==English==
{{wp}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|rĭg}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪɡ/|a=RP,GA,CA,AU}}
** {{audio|en|En-au-rig.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɾɪɡ/|a=Scotland,Wales}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹəɡ/|a=NZ}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪɡ|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From Early Modern English {{m|en|rygge}}, probably of {{der|en|gmq}} origin. Compare {{cog|no|rigge||to bind up; wrap around; rig; equip}}, Swedish dialectal {{m|sv|rigga||to rig a horse}}, Faroese {{m|fo|rigga||to rig; to equip and fit; to make s.th. function}}. Possibly from {{der|en|gem-pro|*rik-||to bind}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*rign-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*reyg-||to bind}}; or related to Old English {{m|ang|*wrīhan}}, {{m|ang|wrīohan}}, {{m|ang|wrēohan}}, {{m|ang|wrēon||to bind; wrap up; cover}}. See also {{l|en|wry||to cover; clothe; dress; hide}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|rigging}} {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[rigging]] of a sailing ship or other such [[craft]].
# [[special|Special]] equipment or [[gear]] used for a particular purpose.
#: {{ux|en|The climbers each had a different '''rig''' for climbing that particular rockface.}}
#: {{ux|en|We used a ground-level '''rig''' to safely learn how to tile a gable roof.}}
# {{senseid|en|large Q43193 especially Q1936841}} {{lb|en|US}} A large [[truck#English:_Q43193|truck]], especially a [[semi-trailer truck#English:_Q1936841|semi-trailer truck]].
#: {{ux|en|Every '''rig''' at the truckstop had custom-made mud-flaps.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1975|lyricist=C.W. McCall; Chip Davis|title={{w|Convoy (song)|Convoy}}|album=Black Bear Road|url=|artist=w:C. W. McCall|passage=There's armored cars, and tanks, and Jeeps<br>And '''rigs''' of every size.<br>Yeah, them chicken coops was full o'bears<br>And choppers filled the skies.}}
# The special [[apparatus]] used for drilling wells.
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[costume]] or an [[outfit]].
#: {{ux|en|My sister and I always made our own '''rigs''' for Halloween.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|computing}} A [[personal computer]], typically one modified for [[looks]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Radford Castro|title=Let Me Play: Stories of Gaming and Emulation|page=104
|passage=When I saw a special version of Quake running on Voodoo hardware, I knew I would be forking out quite a bit of money on my gaming '''rig'''.}}
# An imperfectly castrated [[horse]], [[sheep]] etc.
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[radio|Radio]] equipment, especially a [[CB radio|citizen's band]] [[transceiver]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} Equipment used for taking [[recreational drug]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|author=Reyes Ramos|title=An Ethnographic Study of Heroin Abuse by Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas|page=36
|passage={{...}} does not know how to pick up the liquid from the cooker, and he asks someone else to use his '''rig''' to put his part in his '''rig'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Josiah Howard|title=Cher: Strong Enough
|passage=(Gregg later admitted Cher's inadvertent discovery of his “'''rig'''” [drug bag] complete with heroin, needles, and rubber bands, hastened their breakup.)}}
# {{lb|en|animation}} A model outfitted with parameterized controls for animation.

